+(duration-type)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is either a whole number of seconds, like
+`120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit: `d` for days,
+`h` for hours, `m` for minutes, and `s` for seconds. Each unit may be used at
+most once and units must appear in that order, like `1h30m` or `1d2h3m4s`.
+Units are case-insensitive, and spaces are not allowed.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting for {timeout}")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1h30m"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=90"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=30m1h"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--help"])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.6.0
+```
+
